Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.890
Jim, where are you, what's going on?

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.290
Thanks so much, it is great to be here.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.920
Thank you for having me, Conan.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.600
Oh, for God's sake, don't--
It's good to be here.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.670
I'm a big fan of your,
uh, (clears throat) show.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.900
Okay, you have it on a, it
says show on a piece of paper?

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.530
That's the idea, really?
It says show.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.150
Okay, uh-huh.
Hold on excuse me.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:23.650
Okay.
Yes?

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.960
All right, no, no.
Yes, just a minute.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.170
No, no.
Yes.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.270
You're talking into a zucchini.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.366
Yes, he is wearing the
shirt of a 12-year-old boy.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:36.783
(Conan and Jim laughing)

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.400
We've got a lot to talk about.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.040
We've known each other, I
think for over 60 years.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.293
65.
65 years.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.170
What is that, is that urine in a jar?

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:52.253
I've been busy today.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:58.200
So you're urinating into a jar on Zoom?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.650
These are human eyeballs.
Oh for God...

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:05.650
This is, I had some dilly
beans from Aunt Martie,

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:10.070
a friend of mine who makes,
he sent me some of these,

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:13.720
these dilly beans, amazing.
Okay, okay.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.530
Sorry, go on.
No, no, no, no.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:17.150
This is all gold.
Wait a minute,

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:21.060
who put these stairs here?
Oh, look at that.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.703
You got some stairs there?

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:28.430
It's hard to, that's the
laziest going down stairs

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:29.840
I've ever done because I don't want

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.230
to move out of my chair, and
I don't have the quad strength

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:37.970
so I'm just gonna do it while
remaining in a chair you know?

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.080
It's ridiculous.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:42.210
How are you, Jim, we've
known each other, as I said,

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:45.400
for like 60 years and we've
liked each other for months.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.760
Yes.
How are you holding up

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.660
in quarantine, how are
you doing, old friend?

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:54.590
Yeah, I just want, I'm here with my family

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.560
which I love them dearly.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:01.960
And I just want, I want
someone to go to bed.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.740
I'm tired, nobody goes to sleep.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.620
It used to be people would go to bed.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.130
I'm the only one that goes to bed.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.160
I nap during the day

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:13.120
and I'm still the first one
to go to bed, I'm tired.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:18.120
Yeah, I know you have a very large family.

00:02:18.446 --> 00:02:20.130
How many people we talking here?

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.530
How many kids do you got?

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:26.480
There are five children,
and they're just--

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.050
And no one sleeps, no one goes to bed.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.510
No one actually sleeps.
They don't go to sleep.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.903
They're just, they're like my wife.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:36.020
They don't need sleep, they wanna talk.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:37.030
They wanna do things.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:40.390
It's like, I don't know, I
shouldn't have had a family.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:43.080
I don't know if it's too
late now, but I still...

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.910
No, there's still things you could do.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:48.980
They're not legal, they're not moral,

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.480
but we can talk when
this interview is over.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.620
There's still a way out.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.290
Remember when you told me
you thought Scott Peterson

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.289
was a good guy, you remember that?

00:02:58.289 --> 00:03:01.210
(Conan laughing)

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:05.090
Yeah, yeah, I remember
going on at great length

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:06.160
about how one of the--

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.530
You said that guy who
killed his pregnant wife

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:09.530
was a good guy and I
was like, "No, Conan."

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:12.287
Yeah, I said, "That guy just," I said,

00:03:12.287 --> 00:03:16.160
"He feels like a quality,
quality chum, he does."

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:17.555
That's what I said.
Yeah.

00:03:17.555 --> 00:03:18.859
Do you think that was a mistake?

00:03:18.859 --> 00:03:21.096
I think that's wrong,
do you know what I mean?

00:03:21.096 --> 00:03:23.340
Okay, okay, so what are you doing?

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.532
You're not sleeping.

00:03:24.532 --> 00:03:29.532
You've got at last count 15
kids, a wife that won't sleep.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.520
You must be losing your mind.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.960
Is there anything that gives you peace

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.016
during these strange times we're in, Jim?

00:03:35.016 --> 00:03:37.840
I spend time in my garden.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.760
That never used to happen before.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.820
And you know what I like about my garden

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.803
is my family's not there.

00:03:47.304 --> 00:03:48.137
That's a sweet--

00:03:48.137 --> 00:03:49.366
That's what I like about my garden.

00:03:49.366 --> 00:03:52.440
That's really sweet.
Hold on, hello.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.490
Okay, no.
Yeah.

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:56.821
The interview's, I don't know how long.

00:03:56.821 --> 00:03:59.730
I'm just phoning it in,
don't worry, I'll be done.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.603
Okay, I love you, too.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.900
The zucchini bit, this
is something you're--

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.296
The zucchini bit, I
always go to it, you know.

00:04:07.296 --> 00:04:10.170
You're--
Hold on, hold on, hold on.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:15.170
This is a big phone
call, hello? (chuckles)

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:19.633
Yeah, no, it's not working,
none of the bits are.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.797
No, okay, hold on.

00:04:23.797 --> 00:04:24.940
Can I say something?

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:27.150
Are these, these must be
coming from your garden.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:27.983
Is that right?

00:04:27.983 --> 00:04:30.030
Is that why you have all
these massive vegetables?

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.860
Yes, these are, and by the way,

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.810
do you remember in "Happy Days"

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.660
when Ralph Malph used to
say, "I still got it."

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:38.330
Mm-hmm.
I don't go it.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:41.388
He'd go, "I still got it."
I still got it.

00:04:41.388 --> 00:04:43.270
I don't got it anymore.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.800
Why would a young child be wondering

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.655
if he's still got it anyway?

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:49.488
I just, I don't know.

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:50.670
I don't know how to answer that question

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:54.280
'cause I just noticed that
they put makeup on my face

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:56.430
but I'm wearing a short-sleeved shirt

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.370
and they didn't touch my arms

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:03.370
and the disparity is shocking
between my face and my arm.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.930
This is a clown show here.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:10.659
I'm in an abandoned theater
and I look like Lorenzo Lamas

00:05:10.659 --> 00:05:13.780
except my arms look like
they've had chemotherapy.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.900
I don't know what's
happening and I apologize.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.447
And you're in a steak
restaurant or some kind of--

00:05:17.447 --> 00:05:21.966
I'm in a steakhouse, and
when Wilmer Valderrama

00:05:21.966 --> 00:05:25.730
finds out you took his
shirt, he's gonna be upset.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:28.393
Okay, okay, you win, you win.

